# Paths the Tauri dev watcher must NOT treat as Rust-side changes.
#
# `tauri dev` watches this crate and rebuilds the binary on any file
# change. Vite writes `node_modules/.vite-temp/*` while probing its
# config, and the dev server's own output lands in `web/dist` — both are
# frontend-side churn that the Rust build has no stake in. Without this,
# starting the dev server tripped the watcher, which restarted the app,
# which restarted the dev server: an immediate rebuild loop that ended in
# `script "dev" exited with code 255`.
#
# `web/src` and `web/demo` are here for a different reason: editing the
# UI or a fixture is not a Rust-side change either, and without them every
# one-character tweak rebuilt and relaunched the whole binary — which,
# while tuning demo fixtures, is most of what you do.
#
# Deliberately narrow, and it has to be. Ignoring `web/` wholesale also
# hides the `package.json` the CLI resolves `beforeDevCommand` against,
# which then fails with `Script not found "dev"`.
web/node_modules
web/dist
web/src
web/demo
